---
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Kalaris Labs handles information when you use its website."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy' },
  ]}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-shell">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal / 02</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Effective 28 September 2026</p>
        <p class="page-lede">
          This policy explains what information this website handles, why we use
          it, and the choices available to you.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-copy">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Information you send us</h2>
          <p>
            If you email us, apply to work with us, or submit a contact form, we
            receive the information you provide. This may include your name,
            email address, organisation, message, résumé, portfolio, and any
            other material you choose to send.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Website analytics</h2>
          <p>
            We use PostHog to understand how the website is used only after you
            consent to analytics. When enabled, it may collect page views,
            interactions, device and browser details, approximate location, and
            session information. Sensitive form fields are masked. You can
            change your choice at any time through “Analytics preferences” in
            the footer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Security and technical data</h2>
          <p>
            Our hosting and security providers may process IP addresses, request
            metadata, device information, and security signals to deliver the
            site, prevent abuse, and diagnose failures. The site uses Cloudflare
            infrastructure and Turnstile on protected forms. We may use Sentry
            to receive technical error and performance reports.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>to respond to questions, applications, and press enquiries;</li>
            <li>to operate, secure, and improve the website;</li>
            <li>
              to understand site use when analytics consent is active; and
            </li>
            <li>to comply with law and protect our rights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Service providers</h2>
          <p>
            We share information only as needed with providers that help us run
            the site and communicate, including Cloudflare, PostHog, Sentry, and
            Resend. They process information under their own terms and privacy
            commitments. We do not sell personal information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the
            purpose for which it was collected, including communication,
            security, record-keeping, and legal obligations. Retention periods
            vary by the type of information and service involved.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
          <p>
            You may decline or withdraw optional analytics. You may also ask us
            to access, correct, or delete personal information we hold about
            you, subject to applicable law and necessary exceptions. We may need
            to verify your identity before completing a request.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. International processing</h2>
          <p>
            Our service providers may process information in countries other
            than your own. Where required, we use the safeguards made available
            by those providers and applicable law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Children</h2>
          <p>
            This website is not directed to children under 13, and we do not
            knowingly collect their personal information through the site.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as the site and our services change. For
            privacy questions or requests, email
            <a href="mailto:contact@kalarislabs.com">contact@kalarislabs.com</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
